{%- comment -%}
  Product card — one line of caption, from whatever the merchant points it at.

  **The text is a dynamic source, not a metafield picker.** Shopify has no
  metafield setting type for a section or block schema; what it has is the
  dynamic-source connector on a `text` setting, and inside a static block it
  binds against `closest.product` — the same context the rest of this card
  reads. So a merchant connects this to `custom.total_carat_weight`, or to the
  vendor, or to any product metafield the shop maintains, and the block prints
  it. Typing a literal in the field is the other half of the same control: the
  same line, said the same way, on every card in the row.

  **Repeatable**, because a caption is a list rather than a slot. The carat
  weight and the origin are two facts and want two lines, and neither is more
  the card's business than the other.

  This is what became of the metal caption's second half. It used to read
  "White Gold · 1.0 ct" in a single element, with the metal following the
  swatch pick and the carat weight appended from a metafield. The metal half
  now belongs to `product-card-variants`, which is the block that knows what
  was picked; everything else about the piece is this.

  **The row is held whether or not there is a word in it.** `.card__meta`
  carries `min-height: 1.5em` and always has — that is what keeps a row of
  cards level when one piece has a caption and its neighbour does not, and it
  is why an unconnected block still shows as an empty line rather than
  collapsing. Both halves of the rule matter here: the block is selectable in
  the editor the moment it is added, and the grid does not jump when a
  metafield is missing on one piece.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign value = block.settings.text | strip

  comment
    The suffix is appended only where the source has not said it already — a
    carat weight stored as "1.0" and one stored as "1.0 ct" should both read
    "1.0 ct". Same shape as the caption's own `unless contains 'ct'` test.
  endcomment
  assign suffix = block.settings.suffix | strip
  if value != blank and suffix != blank
    unless value contains suffix
      assign value = value | append: ' ' | append: suffix
    endunless
  endif
-%}

<span class="card__meta" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ value }}</span>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_card_meta.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_meta.text.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_meta.text.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "suffix",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_meta.suffix.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_meta.suffix.info"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_card_meta.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
